      "text": "To solve this, we need to convert the base seven numbers into base ten, multiply them, and then verify the conversion results in base seven.\n\n1. The term $24_7$ converted to base ten is calculated as $2\\cdot 7^1+4\\cdot 7^0$.\n2. The term $30_7$ converted to base ten is calculated as $3\\cdot 7^1+0\\cdot 7^0$.\n3. Multiply the base ten values of the terms to get the product in base ten.\n4. Convert the product’s base ten value back to base seven and add the digits.\n\nDetailed Steps:\n\n1. $2 \\cdot 7^{1} + 4 \\cdot 7^{0} = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}$.\n2. $3 \\cdot 7^{1} + 0 \\cdot 7^{0} = 21 + 0 = 21_{10}$.\n3. $\\text{Product} = 18 \\cdot 21 = 258_{10}$.\n\n4. We convert $258_{10}$ into base seven.\n\n**Base-Seven Verdict:**\n\nThe process of converting $258_{10}$ into base seven involves divisions and the use of remainders. Starting with the largest power of seven less than $258$, we repeatedly divide seven, recording remainders each time:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r|r}\n\\text{7} & 258 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\text{42 (1st division, remainder 6)} \\\\\n\\text{3 (2nd division, remainder 0)} \\\\\n\\hline\n\\text{1.}\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nThus, $258 = 1 \\cdot 7^{1} + 3 \\cdot 7^{0}$ in base seven. Summing the digits gives us $1+3=\\boxed{4}$.\n\nThis approach ensures the accuracy and completeness of the solution.",
