      "text": "To determine the product of the base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) and then find the sum of the digits of the product, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the base seven numbers to base ten:**\n   - \\(24_7\\) can be converted to base ten as follows:\n     \\[\n     24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\n     \\]\n   - \\(30_7\\) can be converted to base ten as follows:\n     \\[\n     30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21_{10}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Multiply the base ten numbers:**\n   \\[\n   18_{10} \\times 21_{10} = 18 \\times 21 = 378\n   \\]\n\n3. **Convert the product back to base seven:**\n   - To convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base seven, we need to repeatedly divide by 7 and record the remainders:\n     \\[\n     378 \\div 7 = 54 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     54 \\div 7 = 7 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 5\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     7 \\div 7 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     1 \\div 7 = 0 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n     \\]\n   - The remainders, read from bottom to top, give us the base seven number:\n     \\[\n     378_{10} = 1050_7\n     \\]\n\n4. **Find the sum of the digits of the product in base seven:**\n   - The base seven number \\(1050_7\\) consists of the digits 1, 0, 5, and 0.\n   - Summing these digits:\n     \\[\n     1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the base seven sum of the digits of the product \\(24_7 \\times 30_7\\) is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
